{"answers":[{"answer":"Approve all 22 requirements as one run.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-9","question":"Should all 22 requirements be approved as one run, or should some requirements be cut?"},{"answer":"Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-10","question":"How should the app handle a feeding save that times out when it cannot reliably tell whether the event was saved?"},{"answer":"Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.","by":"Hamza (via web)","id":"Q-11","question":"Should dashboard and yard-summary aggregates be guaranteed to exclude sample records, even when the service returns aggregates mixed with operational data?"}],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-12","impact":3,"impactReason":"The choice determines how feeding quantities and downstream lot-level consumption and cost are recorded.","options":["Have the user enter a delivered quantity for each lot, with the lot quantities adding up to the pen total.","Allocate the pen total automatically among lots in proportion to their animal counts.","Record a separate feeding event for each lot in the pen."],"reason":"This directly provides the per-lot allocation the requirement calls for without adding an allocation rule.","recommended":"Have the user enter a delivered quantity for each lot, with the lot quantities adding up to the pen total.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"When one pen contains multiple lots, how should the delivered feed quantity be allocated among them?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-13","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines which rations planners may use and whether an approval permission and state are needed.","options":["Require an authorized ration manager to approve a ration before planners can assign it.","Remove the approval requirement; planners may assign any saved ration."],"reason":"The request asks for ration creation and management, but does not ask for an approval workflow.","recommended":"Remove the approval requirement; planners may assign any saved ration.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should ration approval be required before a planner can assign a ration?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-14","impact":3,"impactReason":"The selected financial metric changes the money-related information shown to authorized users.","options":["Show service-returned ROI percentage (net return divided by investment), or show it as unavailable when not returned.","Show service-returned net profit or margin in currency, or show it as unavailable when not returned.","Show cost of gain as the profitability metric."],"reason":"The request specifically asks for lot-level financial ROI, and this makes the displayed metric identifiable without adding client-side calculations.","recommended":"Show service-returned ROI percentage (net return divided by investment), or show it as unavailable when not returned.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Which financial return metric should the lot profitability view identify?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-15","impact":2,"impactReason":"This affects layout and control behavior across viewport sizes, but not data, money, or permissions.","options":["Retain both explicit criteria: no horizontal page overflow and a 44-by-44-pixel minimum target size.","Omit these additional explicit criteria and rely on the responsive, touch-sized baseline."],"reason":"The request does not specify these thresholds, so the smallest scope is to rely on the baseline responsive and touch-friendly requirement.","recommended":"Omit these additional explicit criteria and rely on the responsive, touch-sized baseline.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"Should the explicit no-horizontal-overflow and 44-by-44-pixel minimum target criteria be retained in addition to the responsive, touch-sized baseline?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"AC-11.1 requires a delivered-quantity allocation for every lot in the feeding request, but the user enters only a pen-level delivered quantity and the spec defines no way to choose or derive allocations when a pen contains multiple lots.","reqId":"REQ-11","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"The requirement promises ration approval, but no acceptance criterion covers approving a ration or distinguishing approved from unapproved rations, while REQ-9 allows a planner to select a ration without an approval condition.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-14.3 permits acting on a sale-timing suggestion and AC-14.2 refers to changing a sale date, but no editable sale-date record, permission, or transition is defined apart from a calculated projected ship date.","reqId":"REQ-14","rubric":6,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-19.1 checks only for unspecified 'available profitability values,' so the profitability view can pass without displaying any identifiable financial return, margin, or profit metric even for a user permitted to see profitability.","reqId":"REQ-19","rubric":3,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"AC-13.1 and AC-13.4 require displaying FCR and cost of gain, but specify no unavailable state when a lot has zero or missing weight gain, even though those ratios cannot be defined then and only the ship date has a missing-data path.","reqId":"REQ-13","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The requirement promises that planners can adjust feed plans, but its acceptance criteria test only initial submission and read-only access, while REQ-10 tests updating only plans already flagged for review.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-18.2 says the sex filter is unavailable 'for records' lacking sex even though the filter applies to the report as a whole, leaving mixed known-sex and unknown-sex results without defined filtering or display behavior.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-6.2 covers successful inventory edits, receipts, adjustments, and wastage changes but provides no refusal or failed-save state that keeps the previously confirmed balance visible when one of these stock-changing requests fails.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The import criteria cover previewing available mock records and displaying a submitted import's result, but do not define an empty preview or preview-service failure state, so the user has no specified feedback when source records cannot be selected.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-22.1 passes when the page merely displays sections or links, even if the architecture diagrams, working demo entry point, validation material, and production-readiness assessment promised by REQ-22 are empty or inaccessible.","reqId":"REQ-22","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"}],"lint":[{"blocking":true,"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L9 size","details":"This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","fails":["This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut."],"passed":false},{"blocking":true,"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true},{"blocking":true,"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","fails":[],"hint":"Each Then names what a test reads, using at least one of these words: response, status, returned, row, record, call, request, sent, email, message, error, event, field, value, count, list, file, screen, page, shown, displayed. \"Sign-in succeeds\" fails; \"The response status is 200\" passes.","passed":true},{"blocking":false,"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","fails":[],"passed":true}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":["Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling or overflow, and provide touch controls at narrow widths with a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels."]}},"problemOf":{"Q-12":[1],"Q-13":[2],"Q-14":[4],"Q-15":[5]},"problems":[{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-11","text":"AC-11.1 requires a delivered-quantity allocation for every lot in the feeding request, but the user enters only a pen-level delivered quantity and the spec defines no way to choose or derive allocations when a pen contains multiple lots."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-8","text":"The requirement promises ration approval, but no acceptance criterion covers approving a ration or distinguishing approved from unapproved rations, while REQ-9 allows a planner to select a ration without an approval condition."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-14","text":"AC-14.3 permits acting on a sale-timing suggestion and AC-14.2 refers to changing a sale date, but no editable sale-date record, permission, or transition is defined apart from a calculated projected ship date."},{"kind":"critic","reqId":"REQ-19","text":"AC-19.1 checks only for unspecified 'available profitability values,' so the profitability view can pass without displaying any identifiable financial return, margin, or profit metric even for a user permitted to see profitability."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Ensure every page works at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling or overflow, and provide touch controls at narrow widths with a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels."}],"round":2,"settled":[{"decision":"Should all 22 requirements be approved as one run, or should some requirements be cut? → Approve all 22 requirements as one run.","how":"answered","kind":"lint","problem":"L9 size: This spec has 22 requirements, about 3 runs' worth of work for a feature; approve it as one run or reject with which part to cut.","ref":"Q-9"},{"decision":"How should the app handle a feeding save that times out when it cannot reliably tell whether the event was saved? → Remove the uncertain-save reconciliation requirement; show a timed-out save as unknown and leave retry resolution to the existing service/user workflow.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-11.8–11.9 treats matching event fields in a refreshed activity list as proof of whether a timed-out save succeeded, so an older identical event can be mistaken for the new save and a delayed or omitted event can lead to a duplicate feeding and inventory decrement.","ref":"Q-10"},{"decision":"Should dashboard and yard-summary aggregates be guaranteed to exclude sample records, even when the service returns aggregates mixed with operational data? → Display the returned aggregate values as provided, without a sample-free guarantee.","how":"answered","kind":"critic","problem":"AC-20.7 requires sample-free dashboard and yard-summary totals even when the response mixes sample and operational records, while REQ-15 and REQ-21 require displaying returned summary and aggregate values, leaving no consistent client behavior if those returned aggregates include sample data.","ref":"Q-11"}],"spec":{"assumptions":["Procurement and receiving demo data is imported through a documented mock adapter; a live connector awaits identification of the source system and interface.","Repeated source imports are matched by source identifiers; PO lines and lots can split across lots and pens while retaining allocated animal quantities.","Forecasts use configurable yard target-weight and expected-gain defaults with optional lot-specific overrides.","Configured wastage applies to estimates and projections; actual known wastage is a separate movement, while actual stock consumption is based on delivered quantity.","Ration optimization compares candidate mixes with user-selected nutritional requirements, displays the lowest-cost qualifying mix, and saves only when the user chooses.","A saved plan remains unchanged and is flagged for review after relevant inputs change; an authorized planner confirms or regenerates it.","When stock is insufficient, the feeding save is refused and the web app presents the returned error.","Feed calculations use as-fed quantities; feed totals are converted to pounds for feed-to-gain metrics and dry matter is used for nutrition calculations.","A projected ship date uses the current date plus remaining target weight divided by positive ADG and is unavailable without positive ADG.","Date-range report metrics use feeding and weight records in the selected range; sex is retained when supplied and its filter is unavailable for records without sex data.","Dashboard lot rankings use a user-selected measure; dashboards remain summary-only and lot/report screens provide detail.","Predictive suggestions are explainable rule-based recommendations and do not change saved plans unless a user chooses an action.","Sample records remain distinguishable from operational records, duplicate loading is prevented or surfaced through the returned result, and reset or replacement requires confirmation.","Yard summary ADG and cost of gain use aggregate values across included active lots.","Screen actions and displayed values follow permissions returned for the signed-in user; role descriptions do not establish additional role names or permissions.","Lot profitability is presented as an on-screen filtered list with CSV export rather than a custom report builder.","The API is authoritative for server-side calculations and permissions; the web app displays returned values and refusal messages."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"At viewport widths of 360 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, 100% of pages render without horizontal overflow; interactive controls at 360 px width have a minimum 44-by-44 CSS-pixel target.","text":"Every page shall render responsively at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"At viewport widths 320 px, 768 px, and 1280 px, horizontal page overflow is 0 px; at 320 px width, each touch control is at least 44 × 44 CSS px.","text":"Every web page shall remain usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths without horizontal page scrolling, and touch controls at the narrow viewport shall have a minimum target size of 44 by 44 CSS pixels."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"0 horizontal overflow at viewport widths of 320, 768, and 1440 CSS px; primary touch controls are at least 44 × 44 CSS px at 320 CSS px.","text":"Every web-app page shall render without horizontal page overflow at phone, tablet, and desktop reference widths."}],"outOfScope":["A live procurement-system connector is deferred; the demo uses a documented mock-data import adapter.","Durable persistence and database migration behavior for imported records, mappings, inventory, rations, plans, feeding events, and weight measurements are API-side and not specified by these web requirements.","Authoritative server-side calculation and update rules for inventory movements, ration nutrition and cost, feed-plan quantities, lot rollups, forecast values, and feed-to-gain metrics are not specified by these web requirements.","Authorization enforcement, import identifier matching and deduplication, stock sufficiency decisions, and authoritative yard/profitability data filtering are API-side; these web requirements cover controls, displayed responses, and export contents."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service accepts the submitted credentials and returns the user and permissions","id":"AC-1.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned operational landing page and navigation actions allowed by the returned permissions","when":"The user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"The sign-in screen is displayed and the authentication service refuses the submitted credentials","id":"AC-1.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned error message and remains on the sign-in page","when":"The user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"An authenticated screen displays protected data and the session expires or a protected request receives HTTP 401","id":"AC-1.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen returns to sign-in and no protected page data remains displayed","when":"The web app handles the expired session or 401 response"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide email-and-password sign-in, send the submitted credentials to the sign-in service, display the resulting landing page or authentication error, render navigation and actions according to the signed-in user's returned permissions, and clear authenticated page data and return to sign-in when an authenticated session expires or a protected request returns HTTP 401.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-9","Q-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An operationally authorized user opens the import screen and mock adapter records are available","id":"AC-2.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each available record's vendor, source identifier, cost, head count, animal weight, breed, age, source, purchase-order, and receiving fields","when":"The user previews the source records"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user has selected mock source records","id":"AC-2.2","level":"ui","then":"The import request contains the selected source records and the screen displays the response status, imported-record list, and returned created or updated counts when supplied","when":"The user submits the import"},{"given":"A user without operational access opens the import screen","id":"AC-2.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays imported records and does not show an enabled import action","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"}],"ears":"Where mock procurement and receiving import is available, the feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users preview and submit selected records through the documented mock-data adapter and display the returned import result and source fields.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-1","ASM-23","ASM-24","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An imported PO line is allocated across multiple lots and a lot is allocated across multiple pens","id":"AC-3.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows each PO-line-to-lot and lot-to-pen relationship with its allocated animal quantity","when":"The mapping screen renders the returned mappings"},{"given":"A mapping response contains pen information","id":"AC-3.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each mapped pen's ID, capacity, current animal count, and mapped allocation quantity","when":"The mapping screen renders the response"},{"given":"An operationally authorized user changes mapping quantities, or a user without operational access opens the mapping screen","id":"AC-3.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved mapping values returned by the service, and for a user without operational access it displays existing mappings without mapping-change actions","when":"The authorized user saves mappings or the other user's screen renders using returned permissions"},{"given":"An edited allocation conflicts with a PO line's returned head count or a pen's returned capacity and the mapping service refuses the save","id":"AC-3.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned error and the last saved mapping values remain displayed","when":"The user submits the mapping changes"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let operationally authorized users map PO lines to one or more lots and lots to one or more pens, retain allocated animal quantities, and display the resulting traceability and pen information.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-2","ASM-25","Q-3"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The import response identifies source records as matched to existing records","id":"AC-4.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the matched record list and response status without displaying those records as newly created duplicates","when":"The repeated import completes"},{"given":"A repeated-import response updates a PO line's head count below its existing mapped allocation quantities and returns an allocation conflict","id":"AC-4.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the matched record, returned head count, existing mapped quantities, and an allocation-conflict flag without presenting the record as a new duplicate","when":"The repeated import completes"}],"ears":"When an operational user repeats an import containing previously imported source-system identifiers, the feedlot web app shall display the import result for the matched records returned by the import service without presenting them as newly created duplicates, and flag returned allocation conflicts when an updated head count is below existing mapped quantities.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","ASM-24","Q-3"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The forecast response contains incoming animal data, yard defaults, and a lot-specific override","id":"AC-5.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned incoming data, target weight, expected gain rate, projected market date, and forecast basis using the lot-specific override","when":"A user opens the lot forecast"},{"given":"A lot forecast has no positive gain rate available","id":"AC-5.2","level":"ui","then":"The projected date field displays an unavailable value on the screen","when":"The user opens the forecast"},{"given":"An authorized manager changes a yard default or lot-specific override, or a user without manager authorization opens forecast settings","id":"AC-5.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned forecast values for saved changes, and does not show assumption-edit actions to a user without manager authorization","when":"The manager saves the assumption or the other user's screen renders"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display market-date and target-weight forecasts from incoming animal data and configured yard defaults, use lot-specific overrides when present, show a forecast as unavailable without a positive gain rate, and expose forecast-assumption editing only to authorized managers.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-2","ASM-3","ASM-33","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The inventory response contains feed items and stock movements","id":"AC-6.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays each item's name, category, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, storage location, wastage setting when returned, and opening, received, consumed, and closing stock values","when":"A user opens the inventory screen"},{"given":"An authorized inventory user records a receipt or adjustment, edits an item, or changes wastage settings","id":"AC-6.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the saved inventory record and stock-movement values returned by the service","when":"The user submits the change"},{"given":"A user has inventory viewing access but lacks inventory-edit access","id":"AC-6.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays inventory values and does not show enabled item, receipt, adjustment, or wastage-edit actions","when":"The user opens inventory"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display feed inventory items and stock movements and let authorized inventory users maintain items, record receipts or adjustments, and change wastage settings, while displaying inventory details to users with viewing access.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-28","ASM-34","Q-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The projection response contains available stock, upcoming saved feed plans, and wastage-adjusted estimates","id":"AC-7.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned projected consumption and closing or remaining inventory for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons, along with the configured wastage ratio","when":"A user selects each supported projection horizon"},{"given":"The projection response has no saved upcoming feed plans for an item","id":"AC-7.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the response's empty-data state for that item's projected inventory","when":"A user opens inventory projections"},{"given":"The inventory service returns a known actual-wastage movement and delivered-feed consumption","id":"AC-7.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen lists actual wastage as a separate movement from delivered-feed consumption","when":"A user views the stock movement list"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display inventory projections for daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, semi-annual, and annual horizons using saved upcoming feed plans and configured wastage, while presenting known actual wastage separately from delivered-feed consumption.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-3","ASM-4","ASM-27","ASM-28"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized ration manager creates or revises a ration","id":"AC-8.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays fields for ration name and type, ingredients, proportions, intended animal type or weight range, dry matter, energy, and cost per unit","when":"The manager enters ration details and ingredient proportions"},{"given":"The ration service returns nutrition values and calculated ingredient-mix cost","id":"AC-8.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned nutrition values and calculated cost per pound","when":"The ration screen renders the response"},{"given":"An authorized ration manager 