":"The user views the suggestion"},{"given":"An authorized planner chooses to act on a displayed suggestion","id":"AC-14.3","level":"ui","then":"The change request contains the planner's selected action and the screen displays the response status","when":"The planner submits the corresponding change"},{"given":"A user without planning access views a suggestion or the service refuses that user's attempted plan change","id":"AC-14.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen does not show an enabled plan-change action, or displays the returned refusal error, and the saved feed plan remains unchanged","when":"The user opens lot insights or submits the change request"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall present explainable rule-based suggestions for feeding adjustments or sale timing based on lot weight-gain trends and leave any resulting plan or sale change to an authorized planner's explicit action.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","I-8","I-9","ASM-18","ASM-19"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The dashboard service returns yard, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, weight, and performance values","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays active lot and pen counts, animals per lot and pen, inventory status, ration usage, daily bunk rate per pen, planned versus actual feed, total feed consumed and cost, starting and current weight, total gain, ADG, feed-to-gain ratio, cost per unit of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots","when":"A user opens the dashboard"},{"given":"The dashboard displays best- and worst-performing lot rankings","id":"AC-15.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the lot ranking and selected measure as its basis","when":"The user selects FCR, ADG, or cost of gain as the ranking measure"},{"given":"The dashboard response contains no value for a summary field","id":"AC-15.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned empty-data state for that field","when":"A user opens the dashboard"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display a dashboard of yard and lot performance, inventory, feeding, weight, cost, and energy values and let users select the measure used to rank best- and worst-performing lots.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-14","ASM-22","ASM-36"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The operational report service returns records for multiple pens, lots, rations, feed plans, inventory items, and feed costs","id":"AC-16.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows which pen consumed the most feed, which lot has the best FCR and highest ADG, which ration is used most, planned-versus-actual feed and over- or under-feeding pens, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of weight gain","when":"A user opens the reports screen and applies its available filters"},{"given":"A filtered operational report is displayed","id":"AC-16.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen","when":"The user exports the report as CSV"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide filterable operational reports for inventory, feeding, lot performance, and profitability that answer the requested pen, lot, ration, plan-variance, inventory, and cost-of-gain questions and export the filtered results as CSV.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","ASM-17"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service response contains only records for the user's authorized yards and profitability fields allowed by the user's returned permissions","id":"AC-17.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows only the returned authorized-yard records and permitted profitability fields","when":"The user opens a dashboard or report"},{"given":"A user exports a filtered dashboard or report view","id":"AC-17.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains only the authorized-yard records and profitability fields shown to that user","when":"The export is generated"},{"given":"A dashboard or report displays records or profitability fields and an updated permissions response removes access to some of that data","id":"AC-17.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen no longer displays the records or fields no longer permitted, and a subsequent downloaded file contains only currently permitted records and fields","when":"The web app processes the updated permissions"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display dashboards, reports, and exports using only records and profitability fields returned for the signed-in user's authorized yards and permissions, and remove previously displayed data from view and subsequent exports when returned permissions change.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-9","I-10","Q-1","ASM-14"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The report service returns lot records with weight and feeding data for a selected date range","id":"AC-18.1","level":"ui","then":"The report request contains the selected filters and the screen displays matching lots with ADG, FCR, and cost-of-gain values calculated from records in the selected date range","when":"The user selects date-range, breed, sex, or pen filters"},{"given":"Records without sex data are included in the report result set","id":"AC-18.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the sex filter as unavailable for records without sex data","when":"The user views the sex filter"},{"given":"The user has applied report filters and has export access","id":"AC-18.3","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains the filtered report rows shown on the screen and omits any yard or profitability fields not permitted by returned permissions","when":"The user exports the report as CSV or PDF"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide a feed-to-gain report comparing lot ADG, FCR, and cost of gain, with date-range, breed, sex, and pen filters, and CSV or PDF exports of filtered results subject to the user's returned permissions.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-10","ASM-21","ASM-35","Q-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns profitability rows for yards authorized to the user","id":"AC-19.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays only the returned authorized-yard rows and their available profitability values","when":"The user opens and filters the lot profitability view"},{"given":"The user has applied filters to the authorized lot profitability list","id":"AC-19.2","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains the filtered authorized rows displayed by the screen","when":"The user selects CSV export"},{"given":"The service indicates that the user cannot view profitability values","id":"AC-19.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen hides profitability values","when":"The user opens the lot profitability view"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide a filterable on-screen lot profitability list for authorized yards and display a CSV file containing the filtered authorized results when the user exports the list.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-9","Q-1","ASM-17"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Sample data is available and has not been loaded","id":"AC-20.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the returned sample records with a visible sample-data designation distinguishing them from operational records","when":"An authorized user loads the sample data"},{"given":"Sample data is already loaded or a duplicate load is refused","id":"AC-20.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned duplicate-load result and the returned record list contains no duplicate sample records","when":"A user attempts to load sample data"},{"given":"A user starts a sample-data reset or replacement but has not confirmed","id":"AC-20.3","level":"ui","then":"The screen shows the existing sample records unchanged and the reset or replacement request is not sent","when":"The confirmation dialog is displayed and the user cancels"},{"given":"A user confirms a sample-data reset or replacement","id":"AC-20.4","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned operation status and resulting sample-data list or record count when supplied","when":"The service returns the operation result"},{"given":"A user lacks sample-data management permission and opens the sample-data controls","id":"AC-20.5","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays sample records and does not show enabled load, reset, or replacement actions","when":"The screen renders using the user's returned permissions"},{"given":"The service refuses a sample-data load, reset, or replacement because the user lacks permission","id":"AC-20.6","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned error and the existing sample-data list remains displayed","when":"The user submits the operation"},{"given":"The service response contains sample and operational records for operational reports or inventory totals","id":"AC-20.7","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays report or inventory values based only on operational records and labels any sample records shown as sample data","when":"A user opens one of those operational views"},{"given":"A user exports an operational report or inventory view when the service response contains sample and operational records","id":"AC-20.8","level":"ui","then":"The downloaded file contains operational records only and excludes sample records","when":"The user generates the export"},{"given":"The dashboard or yard-summary response contains aggregate values, including values that may reflect sample and operational records","id":"AC-20.9","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays the returned aggregate values as provided without excluding or recalculating values that may include sample records","when":"A user opens the dashboard or yard summary"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall let an authorized user load visibly distinct sample data, prevent duplicate sample loading while displaying the returned result, require confirmation before sample-data reset or replacement, distinguish sample records from operational records, exclude sample records from operational report and inventory-total views and their exports, and display dashboard and yard-summary aggregate values as returned by the service.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","I-12","ASM-15","ASM-37","Q-11"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The summary service returns active-lot aggregate values","id":"AC-21.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost for the returned active lots","when":"A user with yard-summary access opens the yard summary"},{"given":"The summary service returns no data for one or more summary metrics","id":"AC-21.2","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays returned available values and an explicit unavailable value for each missing field","when":"A user opens the yard summary"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall display a yard-level summary of active-lot total head, average ADG, average cost of gain, and total feed cost using returned aggregate values, and show unavailable values when required source data is missing.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-11","ASM-16","ASM-38"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The delivery overview or presentation page is available","id":"AC-22.1","level":"ui","then":"The screen displays sections or links for the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation, challenges, production readiness, and go-to-market analysis","when":"A user opens the page"}],"ears":"The feedlot web app shall provide a delivery overview or presentation page containing the proposed solution, architecture diagrams, app demo entry point, prompts used, testing and validation overview, challenges, production-readiness assessment, and go-to-market analysis.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-12"],"stability":1}]}}